+# P4-T2: The catalog database: bank albums, merchant patterns and the bank-album route
+
+- **Status:** built and verified locally on `p4/t2-catalog-db`, from `origin/claude/p1a-vault-core` (#457's merge `ab350e48` or later). Not pushed. Under R87 this receipt is its own file; `premium-progress.md` is not edited. Under R100 whole suites are CI's (the full workers suite, the full render suite and its sections, the exports, the database suites and `test:ops`). No app file, Expo route or app entry changed, so `typecheck:routes`, `export:web` and the app's suites are not in the local gate.
+- **Delivers:** `P4:catalog-db`: the `CATALOG_DB` D1 binding, its migrations in `apps/edge/migrations/catalog`, its test setup (as 1C's `AUTH_DB`), the tables `bank_albums` and `merchants` with a draft seed, the merchant reader and matcher for P4-T6, and `GET /v1/catalog/bank-albums`.
+  - `migrations/catalog/0001_catalog.sql`: the plan's two STRICT tables, verbatim. `0002_catalog_seed.sql`: the draft seed (default pending owner Q8, for the owner's review): `K PLUS` (`kbank`), `SCB EASY` (`scb`) and `Krungthai NEXT` (`ktb`), each on `ios` and `android`; merchants `7-eleven` and `เซเว่น` (`food`), `bts` and `mrt` (`travel`), `lotus's`, `big c` and `makro` (`shopping`), each stored as its own `merchantKey`, none GoGoCash-eligible.
+  - `GET /v1/catalog/bank-albums` (`public`, Worker route `catalog.bankAlbums`, an added route, no gate, no release): `{ albums }` of known banks (`isThaiBankKey`), by bank, platform and name, with `etag: "<hex SHA-256 of the body>"`. An `If-None-Match` that names the tag (also weakened, `W/"..."`, or in a list) is 304 with no body and the same tag. Without `CATALOG_DB`: 503 `SERVICE_UNAVAILABLE`, retry 30. No token or client header is needed.
+  - `src/catalog/catalog.ts`: `merchantPatterns(env, nowMs?)` reads `merchants` once an hour per isolate and per binding (A30), `[]` without the binding; a failed read logs `catalog_merchants_failed` (the class name only), answers the last list (or `[]`) and is tried again on the next call. `merchantKey` is NFC, ASCII letters lowered, each run of characters other than letters, marks (`\p{L}\p{M}`: Thai vowels and tone marks stay), digits (`\p{Nd}`, Thai digits included), `-`, `.` and `'` made one space, trimmed. `matchMerchant` compares merchant keys and answers the category key of the longest matching pattern (the first listed wins a tie): a pattern with a Thai character matches anywhere, any other only as whole words; a pattern with nothing left matches nothing; a null name is null.
+  - A29: no `category_packs` table. A30: no KV merchant snapshot. A20 does not apply: P6C-T1 has not landed (`wrangler.jsonc` has no `env.staging` or `env.production` block).
